<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || this.get(i) == null) && (\old(this.get(i)) == null || \old(this.get(i)).equals(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the index is valid (between 0 and the initial size of the list inclusive), then for every valid index before the specified index, each element at that position remains unchanged or is null both before and after the operation.
